course: dictionary
lesson: 10604
title: Undisturbed
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word undisturbed is made of un-, which often means "not", and disturbed, which means bothered or moved. So undisturbed means not bothered, not interrupted, or not moved. Read the words around it to check.
explain: «She slept undisturbed all night.» Nobody woke her or interrupted her, so undisturbed means not interrupted. Test it: "She slept not interrupted all night" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «In undisturbed sedimentary rock, the lowest layers are the oldest.» Here undisturbed means not moved or changed. Rock left in place for a long time keeps its layers in order, with the oldest at the bottom.
fact: Undisturbed means not interrupted, bothered or moved.
fact: «Undisturbed» can mean peaceful, as in «she slept undisturbed.»
fact: «The dust lay undisturbed» means nobody had moved it.
fact: In «undisturbed sedimentary rock», the lowest layers are the oldest, because nothing has moved them.
fact: Useful phrases: sleep undisturbed, leave undisturbed.
exercise: «She slept undisturbed through the storm.» What does undisturbed mean here? | *Not woken or bothered | Noisy and wet | Very tired | Lost in the dark
exercise: «The dust lay undisturbed on the old shelf.» What does undisturbed mean here? | Swept into a pile by the wind | Shiny and clean | *Left where it was, not moved or changed
exercise: «In undisturbed sedimentary rock, the lowest layers are the oldest.» Find and copy the word that tells you the rock was left alone. | *undisturbed | rock | oldest | lowest
test: What does it mean when a forest is undisturbed? | Full of noise and people | *Left alone, with nobody damaging it | Very young and new | Covered in new roads
test: Which sentence uses undisturbed to mean not interrupted? | «The shop was crowded and loud.» | «The dog barked at every car.» | *«He read undisturbed until the bell rang.»
exam: Jayden wants to check the meaning of undisturbed in a sentence. What is a good method? | Guess the opposite and move on | Look only at the first letter | Copy the word without thinking about it | *Swap in "not interrupted or not moved" and see if the sentence still makes sense
